# Rust (daemon)
/daemon/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Go (relay)
/relay/bin/
*.test
*.out

# Generated proto code (regenerate with `make proto`)
/relay/internal/proto/
/daemon/src/gen/

# Generated Control API client (regenerate with `make gen-apiclient`).
# Deliberately not committed: nothing in the product imports it — it exists to
# prove docs/api/openapi.yaml is consumable by a real generator, which `make
# apiclient-check` does by generating, compiling, and asserting against it.
/relay/internal/apiclient/client.gen.go

# proptest regression seeds are deliberately TRACKED (#259). A seed file is a
# counterexample: commit it with the fix so it replays for everyone, and never
# delete one as noise. A seed that encodes a test-oracle bug rather than an engine
# bug may be removed only in the change that fixes the oracle, after the case is
# promoted into a named test.
!/daemon/proptest-regressions/

# Build artifacts
/dist/
/build/

# Local secrets, certs, policy, and state — never commit
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.csr
/relay/*.db
/relay/console-snapshots/
/relay/*.sqlite
*.local.yaml

# Transient workflow scratch: dev-loop, spec-check/drift, decompose. Never committed.
/.dev-loop/
/.spec-check/
/.decompose/

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Relay SQLite store (default ./relay-data/relay.db) — local Node/audit state, never commit
/relay/relay-data/
**/relay-data/

# Dev-fleet host-side state exported by scripts/dev-fleet-mcp.sh: the fleet's CA
# cert and two LIVE control-plane credentials. Never commit.
/.dev-fleet/

# Claude Code's local workspace. Ignore everything by default, then re-include the
# three directories that ARE product: the agent workflow this repo is developed with.
# Cloud routines get a fresh clone and only see what is committed, so the pipeline
# has to live in the tree (see "Routines & merge authority" in AGENTS.md).
#
# `/.claude/*` rather than `/.claude/` because git cannot re-include a path whose
# parent directory is excluded.
#
# worktrees/ stays ignored and must: `git add -A` otherwise stages each one as an
# embedded repository — which git accepts with only a warning, producing a commit
# whose clones silently lack the contents. It nearly landed in a PR twice.
/.claude/*
!/.claude/README.md
!/.claude/commands/
!/.claude/agents/

# Compose interpolation files. Never commit one: Compose reads a `.env` beside a
# compose file silently, so a committed one would change the deployment stack's
# bind addresses on the next pull-and-deploy
# (docs/operations/relay-install.md, section 7).
.env
/deploy/*/.env
